From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nds-ports <nds-ports@localhost>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 14:07:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add Nintendo DS platform

Makefile.nds builds a DSi enhanced .nds with devkitARM and libnds/calico,
with int sized enums like Quake expects and common symbols for the
globals it defines in headers. On top of a few engine changes:

- The game data embedded in the ROM (nitro:/id1) is searched before the
  same directory on the SD card, which gets the config and savegames.
- The DS has 4 MiB of RAM in total, so the minimum memory is 2 MiB. It
  has no network play, so there is one client slot instead of at least
  four, and 1024 particles instead of 2048.
- S_ClearBuffer submits the silence, so a driver that copies the DMA
  buffer doesn't loop old sound during loading.

The platform itself:

- System: Quake runs in a thread with a 256 KiB stack in main RAM, the
  hunk takes all RAM that is left, the console output goes to the bottom
  screen and the no$gba debug output, extra arguments come from
  /data/quake/args.txt. A tick task keeps the tick counter behind
  Sys_FloatTime running.
- Video: the 320x200 frame is scaled to the top screen by the affine
  background hardware, smoothed by a half pixel offset second layer that
  is alpha blended on top (vid_smooth), with the palette in the hardware
  palette.
- Input: the buttons send the keys of the default bindings in game and
  menu keys elsewhere, dragging the stylus looks around.
- Sound: Quake's mixer paints a stereo ring buffer, split into two ring
  buffers that loop on hardware channels panned left and right.
- Speed: the span drawers run from ITCM.
